---
// The questions both versions of the page answer. Each page styles them for
// where they sit: the dark decision panel, or the classic page's own section.
// Beside the decision JSON the first question can point at it; elsewhere it
// can't.
interface Props { beside?: boolean }
const { beside = false } = Astro.props;
---
<details>
  <summary>{beside ? "Who decides this shape?" : "Who decides what a decision looks like?"}</summary>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>The plugin. Each one declares what the agent sends and what comes back, as JSON Schema. <b>JSON is the transport, HTML is the view.</b></p>
    <ol class="flow" aria-label="JSON in, an HTML view for you, JSON out">
      <li><span class="node">agent</span></li>
      <li class="edge"><span>JSON</span></li>
      <li><span class="node you">HTML · you</span></li>
      <li class="edge"><span>JSON</span></li>
      <li><span class="node">agent</span></li>
    </ol>
    <pre class="tree" aria-label="The list plugin's files"><span class="dir">list/</span>
├ manifest.json
├ schemas/payload.schema.json   <i>in</i>
├ schemas/decision.schema.json  <i>{beside ? "out ↑" : "out"}</i>
└ view/index.html               <i>the view</i></pre>
  </div>
</details>
<details>
  <summary>Can I make one for my own work?</summary>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Yes, or have your agent make it. A deploy to approve, alerts to triage, three designs to pick from: whatever needs a person.</p>
    <p class="scaffold"><code>$ pinrail plugins new my_plugin</code><a href="/docs/building/writing/">Write a plugin →</a></p>
  </div>
</details>
<details>
  <summary>Which agents work with it?</summary>
  <div class="answer"><p>Any that can run a command: Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, a CI job, a shell script. Its own instructions say when to stop and ask.</p></div>
</details>
<details>
  <summary>Does anything leave my machine?</summary>
  <div class="answer"><p>No. The app runs its server on loopback, and reviews and decisions stay on your computer. There's no account. Plugin views are sandboxed.</p></div>
</details>
<details>
  <summary>What if I'm away when it asks?</summary>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>The agent waits, even through an app restart. With <code>--timeout</code> it stops waiting (exit 4) and the review stays in your inbox.</p>
    <p>Decide when you're back. The agent picks up your decision with the CLI whenever it next looks:</p>
    <pre class="cli-later"><span class="c">$</span> pinrail wait &lt;id&gt;   <i># your decision</i>
<span class="c">$</span> pinrail show &lt;id&gt;   <i># where it stands</i></pre>
  </div>
</details>
<details>
  <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
  <div class="answer"><p>Nothing. Pinrail is free and open source under the Apache License 2.0. It runs on macOS and Linux and is in early development.</p></div>
</details>
